    Security (Feature 150, US4 — wallet PWA parity). Mounts the SAME shared
    SecurityHome the web shell renders at /app/security, here at /wallet/security.
    A citizen is the same person on both hosts (F136 tier model), so the surface
    is identical: how you sign in / two-factor / recovery, with the assurance
    floor rule and always-notify enforced server-side.

    Distinct from Devices (/devices): Security → Passkeys are WebAuthn *login*
    authenticators; Devices are wallet holder-key delegations (F114/F128). The two
    never cross-link as if equivalent (FR-026).
*@
@page "/security"
@layout MainLayout
@attribute [Authorize]

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using MudBlazor
@using Sorcha.UI.Core.Components.Security

<PageTitle>Security · Sorcha Wallet</PageTitle>

<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Small" Class="mt-4">
    <SecurityHome />
</MudContainer>
